course: dictionary
lesson: 14903
title: Getting better with recuperation
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Recuperation is a noun. It is the time when you get better and stronger after an illness, an injury or a tiring time. You will often see it in health stories and sports reports.
explain: «After her operation, Maya needed a long period of recuperation at home.» Look at the clue words around it: operation, home and needed. They show that Maya was not better yet and was healing. So recuperation means the healing time.
explain: «The footballers had two quiet days for recuperation before the big match.» Here it means rest after hard training. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence: rest would fit, so recuperation is the rest that helps the body get strong again.
fact: Recuperation is a noun, so it names a thing: the time or process of getting better.
fact: «Recuperation» means getting better and stronger after an illness, injury or tiring time.
fact: Less common: «recuperation» can also mean getting back something lost, such as energy or money.
fact: Useful phrases: «a period of recuperation», «time for recuperation», and «rest and recuperation», often shortened to R and R.
fact: Clue words such as «ill», «operation», «rest» and «heal» tell you that recuperation is about healing.
exercise: «After her operation, Maya needed a long period of recuperation.» What does recuperation mean here? | A quick trip to the shops | Getting ready for a long race | *Getting better after an operation | Losing her way home
exercise: «The footballers had two quiet days for recuperation before the big match.» What is the recuperation? | A new kit for the match | *Rest after hard training | Extra training every morning | A visit from the referee
exercise: Which word in «The doctor said Sam's recuperation would take three weeks.» is a clue that it is about health? | Week | *Doctor | Said | Three
test: «Grandma spent a month in bed during her recuperation after the fall.» What is her recuperation? | Packing a suitcase | A new bed for the bedroom | A holiday at the seaside | *Getting better after an injury
test: What is the short form of «rest and recuperation»? | *R and R | S and S | A and E | P and P
exam: Which sentence uses recuperation correctly? | *The runner needed two days of recuperation after the marathon. | The recuperation was a loud, red bicycle. | We had recuperation for lunch at the park. | The recuperation ran to the shop for apples.
